Article 3
The objectives of implementing protection for women against acts of violence are: to prevent all forms of violence against women;
to take action against perpetrators of violence against women in accordance with applicable laws and regulations;
to provide integrated protection and services to women victims of gender-based violence occurring in households and/or public spaces in the Paser Regency area.

CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 4
Regional government in implementing the protection of women from acts of violence has the following obligations: to formulate strategic plans for the protection of women against acts of violence for the short, medium, and long term as an integrated part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD);
to prevent and handle in an integrated manner the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to encourage the responsibility of police institutions, prosecutorial institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, religious institutions, and the general public to coordinate and cooperate in preventing and handling the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to optimize the role and function of institutions within the regional government environment related to preventing and handling the protection of women from acts of violence;
to provide facilities and infrastructure;
to conduct guidance, supervision and evaluation.

CHAPTER X
PROHIBITION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN
Article 24
Every person is prohibited from committing violence against women both within the household and/or outside the household, by means of: physical violence;
psychological violence;
verbal violence;
sexual violence; or neglect.

Article 8
Prevention as referred to in article 5 letter a, includes: collecting data and information about women victims of violence and legislation;
conducting education on anti-violence values toward women;
socializing legislation related to the implementation of protection for women victims of violence;
establishing and facilitating the implementation of integrated service institutions for women victims by involving community elements;
encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for women victims of violence;
Increasing women's awareness of the importance of complying with ethics, religious norms and cultural norms in behavior.
Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the District Regional Government, police institutions, prosecution institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, and the community in accordance with their duties, functions, and responsibilities.

BAB IV
SCOPE
Article 5
The implementation of protection of women from acts of violence includes: prevention;
handling;
empowerment.

Article 28
Sexual violence as referred to in Article 24 letter d, includes: forced sexual relations committed against women residing within the scope of the household or outside the household;
forced sexual relations against women within the scope of the household or outside the household with other persons for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes;

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of women is carried out with regard to religion, customs, and the social-culture of the community by prioritizing the basic principles of women's rights.
Protection of women includes efforts to protect and provide a sense of security to women by fulfilling their rights, namely through empowerment to improve the quality of life of women through improvement of the physical and mental conditions of women in fulfilling their rights and life needs as part of human rights.
The implementation of protection of women victims of violence is based on the principles of: Respect for the rights of victims;
Justice and gender equality;
Non-discrimination;
The best interests of victims.

